            { title: "ICC (A) — All Risks", content: `<p>The broadest marine coverage. Covers ALL risks of loss or damage except specific exclusions.</p><h4>Risks Covered:</h4><ul><li>Fire, explosion, lightning</li><li>Vessel sinking, capsizing, grounding, stranding</li><li>Collision of vessel or craft with any external object</li><li>Overturning or derailment of land conveyance</li><li>Earthquake, volcanic eruption</li><li>Washing overboard, jettison</li><li>Entry of sea/lake/river water into vessel or container</li><li><strong>Theft, pilferage, non-delivery</strong></li><li><strong>Breakage, leakage, wetting, contamination</strong></li><li><strong>Hook damage, denting, scratching</strong></li><li><strong>Fresh/rain water damage</strong></li><li>General average and salvage charges</li></ul><h4>Exclusions:</h4><ul><li>Wilful misconduct of the insured</li><li>Ordinary leakage, wear and tear</li><li>Insufficiency of packing</li><li>Inherent vice of goods</li><li>Delay</li><li>War, strikes (separate cover available)</li></ul><div class="ins-highlight">Mandatory under CIP Incoterm. Recommended for high-value goods, electronics, fragile items.</div>` },
            { title: "ICC (B) — Named Perils", content: `<p>Intermediate coverage. Only specifically listed perils are covered.</p><h4>Risks Covered:</h4><ul><li>Fire or explosion</li><li>Vessel stranding, grounding, sinking, capsizing</li><li>Overturning or derailment of land conveyance</li><li>Collision with external object (not water)</li><li>Discharge of cargo at port of distress</li><li>Earthquake, volcanic eruption, lightning</li><li>Washing overboard</li><li>Entry of sea/lake/river water into vessel</li><li>Total loss of package during loading/unloading</li><li>General average and jettison</li></ul><h4>NOT Covered:</h4><ul><li>Theft, pilferage, non-delivery</li><li>Rain/fresh water damage</li><li>Breakage, denting, scratching</li><li>Wetting by sweat/condensation</li><li>Contamination, hook damage</li></ul><div class="ins-highlight">Suitable for raw materials, steel, timber — goods not easily stolen or damaged by water.</div>` },
            { title: "ICC (C) — Major Perils Only", content: `<p>Narrowest coverage. Only catastrophic marine events covered.</p><h4>Risks Covered:</h4><ul><li>Fire or explosion</li><li>Vessel stranding, grounding, sinking, capsizing</li><li>Overturning or derailment of land conveyance</li><li>Collision with external object (not water)</li><li>Discharge at port of distress</li><li>General average sacrifice and jettison</li></ul><h4>NOT Covered:</h4><ul><li>Earthquake, volcanic eruption, lightning</li><li>Washing overboard</li><li>Entry of sea water into vessel</li><li>Theft, breakage, wetting, contamination</li><li>Loading/unloading losses</li></ul><div class="ins-highlight">Minimum level required under CIF. Used for low-value bulk cargo (coal, ore, grains).</div>` },
            { title: "ITC (A) — Inland All Risks", content: `<p>Comprehensive coverage for goods in domestic transit by road, rail, or inland waterway.</p><h4>Risks Covered:</h4><ul><li>All risks of physical loss or damage from external causes</li><li>Road accidents — collision, overturning, jackknifing</li><li>Fire and explosion</li><li>Theft of entire consignment or pilferage</li><li>Water damage — rain, flood, river overflow</li><li>Breakage, denting, scratching during handling</li><li>Loading and unloading damage</li><li>Bridge collapse, landslide, derailment</li><li>Non-delivery of entire package</li></ul><h4>Exclusions:</h4><ul><li>Wear and tear, gradual deterioration</li><li>Inherent vice (natural spoilage)</li><li>Insufficient packing</li><li>Delay, loss of market</li></ul><div class="ins-highlight">Recommended for ALL Indian inland movements. Essential given road conditions, theft risk, and monsoon flooding.</div>` },
            { title: "ITC (B) & ITC (C) — Limited Inland", content: `<p><strong>ITC (B)</strong> covers named perils: fire, overturning, collision, flood, storm, cyclone, earthquake, landslide, bridge collapse. Does NOT cover theft, breakage, or rain damage.</p><p><strong>ITC (C)</strong> is bare minimum: only fire, overturning, and collision of carrying vehicle. Does NOT cover natural disasters, theft, water damage, or loading damage.</p><div class="ins-highlight">ITC (B): Acceptable for resilient goods on safe routes. ITC (C): Only for very low-value bulk cargo. In India, ITC (A) is strongly recommended due to road conditions and weather risks.</div>` }
